{
  "slug": "rpm-relentless-product-manager",
  "name": "Rpm Relentless Product Manager",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "rpm persists project state across Claude Code sessions and prevents guidance and documentation drift.\n\nIt uses hooks to automate most of the effort, and stores everything in human readable files.\n\nUser initiated /audit command catches drift in three tiers: mechanical scan, scored subagent review, and full project review.\n\nAll implemented with zero dependencies and all bash.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **8 skills**, **3 agents** and **8 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (8): `audit` (On-demand audit), `backlog` (Manage the rpm backlog (long-term project tasks in docs/rpm/future/tasks.org — distinct from Claude's native TaskCreate list, which is…), `init-rpm` (rpm project setup and verification), `next` (One-step rpm orchestrator, or a bounded internal sequence when given a count or scope), `research` (Exhaustive multi-agent research on any topic), `rpm` (Explain the rpm plugin and list its commands), `session-end` (End the current rpm session), `version` (Report the installed rpm plugin version)\n- **Agents** (3): `auditor` (Background agent that scans project documentation for staleness, contradictions, broken references, and session drift), `guidance-aligner` (Read-only agent that classifies project memory rules (feedback_*.md, MEMORY.md) against active directive docs (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, skill bodies)), `preflight` (Preflight agent for /next)\n- **Hooks** (8): `SessionStart`, `SessionEnd`, `PreCompact`, `PostCompact`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`, `TaskCreated`, `TaskCompleted`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install rpm-relentless-product-manager@claude-community` from `dppdppd/rpm`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 8,
    "agent": 3,
    "hook": 8
  },
